messages:   56%|#####6    | 280/500 [03:44<02:53,  1.27it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 749607278 and 426850538?', "<think>\nI need to add the two numbers 211,325,562 and 970,744,984.\n\nFirst, I'll align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, I'll add each corresponding pair of digits, carrying over any excess to the next higher place value as needed.\n\nAfter adding all the digits, I'll combine the results to get the final sum.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nWe need to find the sum of the two numbers:\n\n\\[\n749,\\!607,\\!278 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 426,\\!850,\\!538\n\\]\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}749,\\!607,\\!278 \\\\\n+\\,426,\\!850,\\!538 \\\\\n\\hline\n1,\\!176,\\!457,\\!816 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Breakdown:**\n\n1. **Add the units place:**\n   \\[\n   8 + 8 = 16 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 6 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Add the tens place:**\n   \\[\n   7 + 3 + 1 (\\text{carry}) = 11 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Add the hundreds place:**\n   \\[\n   2 + 5 + 1 (\\text{carry}) = 8 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 8)\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Add the thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   7 + 0 = 7 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 7)\n   \\]\n   \n5. **Add the ten-thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   6 + 5 = 11 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n6. **Add the hundred-thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   0 + 8 + 1 (\\text{carry}) = 9 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 9)\n   \\]\n   \n7. **Add the millions place:**\n   \\[\n   9 + 6 = 15 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 5 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n8. **Add the ten-millions place:**\n   \\[\n   4 + 2 + 1 (\\text{carry}) = 7 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 7)\n   \\]\n   \n9. **Add the hundred-millions place:**\n   \\[\n   7 + 4 = 11 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n10. **Add the billions place:**\n    \\[\n    0 + 0 + 1 (\\text{carry}) = 1 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1)\n    \\]\n\nCombining all the results, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,\\!176,\\!457,\\!816}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
